					<!-- p class="post-info">Mar 27th, 2009 by <a href="http://remembrance.sufipaths.net/?author=3" title="Posts by khushi" rel="author">khushi</a> </p -->
					<p class="post-meta"><ul class='post-meta'>
<li><span class='post-meta-key'>Birth Date:</span> August 29, 1940</li>
<li><span class='post-meta-key'>Urs date:</span> May 26, 2008</li>
</ul>
</p>
				</div>
				
				<div class="entry">
					<p><img class="aligncenter size-medium wp-image-580" title="arjuna-salim-gerard-lange-2" src="wp-content/uploads/2009/03/arjuna-salim-gerard-lange-2-211x300.jpg" alt="arjuna-salim-gerard-lange-2" width="211" height="300" /></p>
<p>Honorary murshid Arjuna Lange has been a sufi since his birth in a sufi family. All his life he was spreading the Message of Love, Harmony and Beauty. His most important question in his life and what he taught his mureeds, was: What says your heart? That was his leading motive in life.<br />
His heart was open for so many people in his work as a psychiatrist and psychotherapist and in his work within the Sufi Movement as a healer, as conductor of the Confraternity, as cherag and speaker in the Universal Worship, as leader of the cherags and so on, and so on. He was openminded in the psychiatry and in his spiritual life. He always looked with fresh eyes at oldfashioned habits. His inspiration is missed by so many people. May he be home by his Source of light and love.</p>
	
				       				
																					
